#!/usr/bin/env python3
#
# z13-power-settings — settings window for the ASUS ROG Flow Z13 (GZ302).
#
# Standalone PyQt6 window that replaces the z13gui overlay drawer. Launched from
# the z13-power-service tray menu (Settings…) or via `z13-power settings`.
# Everything is a thin wrapper over z13ctl:
#   - Lighting:   apply / brightness / off (keyboard + lightbar, two zones)
#   - Fan curve:  fancurve --get / --set / --reset (8-point curve)
#   - Battery:    batterylimit --get / --set (charge cap 40–100; saved and
#                 re-applied at login — ACPI does not keep it across reboot)
#   - Tweaks:     paneloverdrive, bootsound, CPU undervolt (Curve Optimizer)
#   - Telemetry:  live status readouts (APU temp, fan RPM, profile, TDP)
#   - Profiles:   service.conf [service] section (AC/battery/low-battery modes)
#
# Lighting selections are saved to ~/.config/z13-power/lighting.conf; the tray
# service re-applies them at login.
#
# Usage:  z13-power-settings
#
# Requires: z13ctl, python-pyqt6.

